gRCAi Client Security Guarantee

Trust Boundary

The gRCAi client operates inside a trusted environment.
All external AI reasoning occurs outside this boundary.

The client never transmits raw operational data outside the machine.

⸻

Data Handling Principle

gRCAi is a diagnostic reasoning system, not a log export system.

The client converts operational signals into behavioral observations before persistence and before transmission.

The system is designed so that:

External services receive system behavior, not system data.

⸻

What Never Leaves the Machine

The client is designed to prevent storage or transmission of:

Identity Information
	•	Usernames
	•	Emails
	•	Customer identifiers
	•	Session identifiers
	•	Tenant identifiers

Infrastructure Information
	•	IP addresses
	•	Hostnames
	•	Network topology
	•	Internal URLs and endpoints

Secrets
	•	Passwords
	•	API keys
	•	Tokens
	•	Certificates
	•	Connection strings
	•	Private keys

Operational Content
	•	Raw logs
	•	Request payloads
	•	Query parameters
	•	File contents
	•	Full stack traces

⸻

What May Leave the Machine

Only abstract diagnostic observations are exported, such as:
	•	error categories
	•	dependency failures
	•	retry patterns
	•	latency spikes
	•	resource pressure
	•	availability state
	•	protocol outcomes
	•	component relationships
	•	aggregated counts and rates
	•	timestamps (without identity linkage)

This data describes how the system behaved, not who used it or what data it processed.

⸻

LLM Interaction

The client does not directly interact with any LLM during normal operation.

Instead:

    Client → Sanitized Observations → Central Reasoning Service → LLM

The LLM never receives raw logs from the client machine.

(Local LLM usage exists only in explicit developer mode.)

⸻

Storage Safety

Evidence files generated by the client are designed to be:
	•	safe to share externally
	•	safe to attach to support tickets
	•	safe to include in backups
	•	free of personal or customer data

⸻

Security Model

The system follows pre-collection reduction, not post-collection masking.

Therefore privacy does not depend on:
	•	regex masking correctness
	•	pattern completeness
	•	secret detection heuristics

Sensitive data is avoided by design rather than filtered after the fact.

⸻

Intended Outcome

Even in the event of:
	•	disk compromise
	•	snapshot access
	•	vendor sharing
	•	misconfiguration
	•	AI provider breach

no customer or operational confidential data should be exposed from gRCAi evidence.
